     "<div><div style=\"color:#000;background-color:#fff;font-family:verdana,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\"><div>Dear all,</div><div><br></div><div>I am trying to make some boxplots of a variable (organic carbon) and based on the three different seasons for each year. </div><div><br></div><div>I have a dataframe of 272 observations. </div><div><br></div><div>SYEAR         SEASON        DOC</div><div>1998             cold            1.43</div><div>1998             cold            2.79</div><div>1998             middle        1.83</div><div>1998             middle        1.83</div><div>1998             cold            1.57</div><div dir=\"ltr\">1998             middle        1.57</div><div>....                ....             ...</div><div>2012              warm         4.12</div><div dir=\"ltr\">2012              warm         3.81</div><div>2012              cold           8.25</div><div>2012              middle       4.46<br><br></div><div dir=\"ltr\">Here is my code:<br></div><div dir=\"ltr\"><br></div><div dir=\"ltr\">p&lt;-ggplot(df, aes(SYEAR, DOC))+geom_boxplot(aes(x=SYEAR, y=DOC, fill=SEASON))</div><div dir=\"ltr\">p+xlab(&quot;YEAR&quot;)+ylab(&quot;Dissolved Organic Carbon&quot;)</div><div><br></div><div dir=\"ltr\">but I don&#39;t get the boxplots for each year and each season. </div><div><br></div><div dir=\"ltr\">I have also attached a reproducible example in case you want to go through this yourself. I hope that you can help me on this.</div><div><br></div><div>Thank you in advance. </div><div><br></div><div>Kind regards,</div><div>Maria</div></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
